     aaccppii__wwmmii — ACPI to WMI mapping driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following line in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee aaccppii__wwmmii

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           acpi_wmi_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aaccppii__wwmmii driver provides an interface for vendor specific WMI imple‐
     mentations (e.g. HP and Acer laptops).  It creates /dev/wmistat%d, which
     can be read to get information about GUIDs found in the system.

FFIILLEESS
     /dev/wmistat%d  WMI status device.

